      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5dcad3d53e42912602da0a52|full_name}: Gonna be honest, but i dont agree. If people's login info are just being thrown around like pieces of paper in the wind without even any sort of encryption, then people really should know about it. Especially if it hasn't been addressed in a long time. Thats how people get their account hijacked. And even worse for them if they have the same passsord for multiple accounts, which is already a bad idea.\n\nThe more people that know, the more pressure to do something about it.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
